WEBVTT

00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:21.630
What the hell is that huge thing?!

00:00:21.630 --> 00:00:23.230
I heard that it went out of control

00:00:23.230 --> 00:00:26.540
and escaped from the storage
hangar at the Ministry of Defense.

00:00:26.540 --> 00:00:30.540
There'd be a big mess if you
broke their property.

00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:33.570
Don't be ridiculous! Boomers are boomers!

00:00:36.750 --> 00:00:39.180
Damn! Why can't we shoot?!

00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:42.220
Nene seems to be unable to leave the office,

00:00:42.220 --> 00:00:44.550
and Linna is currently far from here.

00:00:44.550 --> 00:00:48.510
Oh, I forgot to tell you. She might
not be coming back.

00:01:01.840 --> 00:01:06.840
I'm sure it'll take at least an hour
from here to Kumamoto Station.

00:01:06.840 --> 00:01:09.180
Even if I take the Metro Express, it would be...

00:01:09.180 --> 00:01:12.080
What's the matter? Why don't we go to dinner?

00:01:12.080 --> 00:01:13.640
But I...

00:01:14.890 --> 00:01:19.990
Well, I think things will be okay
even if I'm not there,

00:01:19.990 --> 00:01:22.490
because it used to be like that all the time.

00:01:22.490 --> 00:01:25.630
I'd like to have a long talk about it.

00:01:25.630 --> 00:01:27.220
Well, shall we go?

00:01:36.270 --> 00:01:39.810
Command RF, groups three and
five have taken up positions.

00:01:39.810 --> 00:01:42.450
Approval to attack has not been
cleared. Please wait.

00:01:42.450 --> 00:01:45.380
Roger. Please keep the circuit in S mode as it is.

00:01:45.380 --> 00:01:48.290
Wait a second! This is the
AD Police Information Center.
Currently, the target has stopped.
Please confirm it again.

00:01:48.290 --> 00:01:49.720
Wait a second! This is the
AD Police Information Center.

00:01:49.720 --> 00:01:53.660
We've requested an increase in
police to speed evacuation!

00:01:53.660 --> 00:01:56.250
A boomer at the Ministry of Defense?!

00:02:04.870 --> 00:02:05.840
What?!

00:02:08.070 --> 00:02:11.510
See? They want to take care of
their own business by themselves.

00:02:11.510 --> 00:02:13.770
Damn, they're worse than we are!

00:02:21.620 --> 00:02:22.590
Sylia!

00:02:22.590 --> 00:02:25.060
Priss is about to take action. Please handle this.

00:02:25.060 --> 00:02:26.390
Roger!

00:02:26.390 --> 00:02:28.460
This is just like war.

00:02:28.460 --> 00:02:30.760
I have a feeling that we might
not be able to handle this,

00:02:30.760 --> 00:02:33.660
but I can't believe a boomer
like this went insane.

00:02:35.670 --> 00:02:40.740
An evacuation order to civilians
is effective in the G3 area.

00:02:40.740 --> 00:02:43.110
The details of the incident aren't clear,

00:02:43.110 --> 00:02:45.440
but the AD Police are deploying on a large scale,

00:02:45.440 --> 00:02:46.910
and the boomer on the run is...

00:02:53.980 --> 00:02:57.420
I'm so sorry, but I have to go now!

00:02:58.820 --> 00:03:02.660
I'm really sorry. Mr. Masaki, I
understand you're a good man,

00:03:02.660 --> 00:03:04.930
and I'm happy to have gotten to know you.

00:03:04.930 --> 00:03:07.200
I've been breathing the air of
my hometown for a while,

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:09.260
and I've been kind of woolgathering.

00:03:10.370 --> 00:03:12.600
It's what you want to do, isn't it?

00:03:18.410 --> 00:03:21.950
I think I understand you somehow.

00:03:21.950 --> 00:03:25.550
Sometimes you can't do things right,

00:03:25.550 --> 00:03:30.420
and I think it might not be a good
idea to come back home.

00:03:30.420 --> 00:03:33.050
Thank you. You're as kind as I thought.

00:03:34.460 --> 00:03:38.230
I realize I'm about to ask you a big favor...

00:03:38.230 --> 00:03:39.700
What is it?

00:03:42.030 --> 00:03:45.900
I'm sure he hates me since I
borrowed money from him.

00:03:50.240 --> 00:03:51.710
Priss!

00:04:03.720 --> 00:04:04.290
They got it!

00:04:04.290 --> 00:04:07.360
Geez, this place is not a battlefield!

00:04:07.360 --> 00:04:09.030
At least ten houses are smashed.

00:04:09.030 --> 00:04:10.490
Look!

00:04:25.080 --> 00:04:28.450
A machine gets out of control and goes insane.

00:04:28.450 --> 00:04:30.240
Just what is a boomer?!

00:04:52.740 --> 00:04:55.640
I don't care! Attack! Fire Bee!

00:04:57.840 --> 00:04:59.380
I'll take all responsibility!

00:04:59.380 --> 00:05:01.570
This work belongs to the AD Police!

00:05:07.620 --> 00:05:09.320
Damn! It's a machine of war.

00:05:09.320 --> 00:05:11.190
I'm sure it has anti-aircraft missiles!

00:05:11.190 --> 00:05:12.390
What did you say?!

00:05:12.390 --> 00:05:14.320
Fire Bee, evacuate!

00:05:20.030 --> 00:05:21.400
Oh my god!

00:05:29.810 --> 00:05:31.430
The Knight Sabers!

00:05:35.280 --> 00:05:36.370
Bye bye.

00:05:45.960 --> 00:05:48.550
Nene, Sylia can't get in there!

00:05:50.730 --> 00:05:52.730
It's no good! No matter what happens,

00:05:52.730 --> 00:05:55.270
Genom doesn't intend to show
the specs of that boomer!

00:05:55.270 --> 00:05:55.930
Then...

00:05:55.930 --> 00:05:58.030
The only thing we can do is hack
into the Ministry of Defense.

00:05:58.030 --> 00:06:01.200
No way! Stop it! We might get in big trouble!

00:06:01.200 --> 00:06:03.300
You don't see anything here, do you?

00:06:04.810 --> 00:06:06.280
Priss...

00:06:07.440 --> 00:06:10.810
Why?! Get out of my way!

00:06:10.810 --> 00:06:14.350
My house is right there! I want to
know what my family is doing now!

00:06:14.350 --> 00:06:16.350
All traffic here is prohibited now.

00:06:16.350 --> 00:06:18.250
If you keep agitating us like this,
you'll be placed under arrest.

00:06:18.250 --> 00:06:19.660
Don't be ridiculous! Get out!

00:06:19.660 --> 00:06:20.880
Oh my god...

00:06:34.270 --> 00:06:37.030
What the hell? Why isn't the core there?!

00:06:39.510 --> 00:06:41.940
This is pretty difficult, but not
as difficult as Genom.

00:06:53.490 --> 00:06:54.620
What is that?

00:06:54.620 --> 00:06:56.060
A Parasite Bomb.

00:06:56.060 --> 00:06:58.830
It's a virus that shoots high
voltage electricity in a server.

00:06:58.830 --> 00:07:01.360
I saved it when this virus was sent here.

00:07:01.360 --> 00:07:03.630
You're sending it to the Ministry of Defense?!

00:07:03.630 --> 00:07:07.900
Right before all functions stop, the
firewall will open for a moment,

00:07:07.900 --> 00:07:10.070
and at that moment, I'll suck
up all their data at once!

00:07:10.070 --> 00:07:12.940
Hey, I'm not watching you, and
I don't hear anything, okay?

00:07:12.940 --> 00:07:14.200
GO!

00:07:19.580 --> 00:07:21.450
Where's the core?!

00:07:26.120 --> 00:07:27.490
Where do I attack?!

00:07:27.490 --> 00:07:31.230
Wait a second! Nene is trying
to pull the information!

00:07:31.230 --> 00:07:32.250
Priss!

00:07:35.970 --> 00:07:39.160
This might be too much to handle
alone. My meter's almost out.

00:07:46.180 --> 00:07:48.640
Hurry up and die!

00:08:07.100 --> 00:08:10.230
I can't believe we're covering the Knight Sabers!

00:08:10.230 --> 00:08:11.290
Priss!

00:08:17.440 --> 00:08:18.630
Linna!

00:08:39.260 --> 00:08:40.660
Speed it up 10 seconds!

00:08:41.930 --> 00:08:43.570
Speed it up 10 seconds!

00:08:43.570 --> 00:08:45.030
Here it is!

00:08:47.840 --> 00:08:48.910
I see!

00:08:48.910 --> 00:08:52.310
No matter how big, all boomers
have some standard specs.

00:08:52.310 --> 00:08:55.880
That huge body is a kind of powered suit!

00:08:55.880 --> 00:08:58.010
I thought you weren't witnessing anything.

00:09:00.120 --> 00:09:02.550
Priss, we can't do anything
right now. Withdraw now!

00:09:03.720 --> 00:09:04.910
Damn it!

00:09:11.690 --> 00:09:14.730
Urgent message to the
AD Police Command Team!

00:09:14.730 --> 00:09:17.530
The location of the core has been identified!

00:09:25.980 --> 00:09:27.540
I wish she could have found it earlier.

00:09:27.540 --> 00:09:29.310
Priss!

00:09:33.750 --> 00:09:35.150
There she is!

00:09:35.150 --> 00:09:35.950
Who?

00:09:35.950 --> 00:09:37.920
Nothing!

00:09:41.760 --> 00:09:42.880
Priss, look out!

00:09:44.030 --> 00:09:44.990
Come on!

00:10:05.010 --> 00:10:06.250
You're pretty late!

00:10:06.250 --> 00:10:07.850
You've been waiting for me, haven't you?

00:10:07.850 --> 00:10:08.910
Let's go.

00:10:20.400 --> 00:10:22.300
That's enough!

00:10:55.370 --> 00:10:56.800
That was close!

00:10:56.800 --> 00:10:59.000
Nene gave us the information, so...

00:10:59.000 --> 00:11:00.640
Well, let's go home.

00:11:00.640 --> 00:11:02.100
Sure.

00:11:07.380 --> 00:11:13.180
What's going on, Mason? We can't
control the media anymore!

00:11:13.180 --> 00:11:17.150
Why didn't you do something
before it became such a mess?!

00:11:17.150 --> 00:11:21.520
That boomer is a top secret
at the Ministry of Defense.

00:11:21.520 --> 00:11:24.190
We can't do anything on our
own without approval.

00:11:24.190 --> 00:11:29.100
What were the AD Police doing
while the damage was spreading?!

00:11:29.100 --> 00:11:34.470
You know I've been opposed
to militray boomers!

00:11:34.470 --> 00:11:38.780
The company needed to do so for
our boomer division to survive.

00:11:38.780 --> 00:11:41.040
I thought you left these things to me.

00:11:41.040 --> 00:11:44.450
You know how hard I've tired

00:11:44.450 --> 00:11:49.540
to get people to accept boomers
as friends of humanity.

00:12:10.510 --> 00:12:12.710
This is a nice chair, isn't it?

00:12:12.710 --> 00:12:17.880
You're displaying your business
savvy as the owner of Genom.

00:12:17.880 --> 00:12:20.940
It's an impossible dream come
true for an ordinary man.

00:12:22.050 --> 00:12:24.020
Shall I move you here?

00:12:24.020 --> 00:12:27.290
No thanks. I know I'm not the type
who fits such a position.

00:12:27.290 --> 00:12:30.360
The only thing I want is to get paid appropriately.

00:12:30.360 --> 00:12:34.230
It was difficult for me to exchange
the core of the military boomer.

00:12:39.040 --> 00:12:41.100
Now it's clear.

00:12:41.100 --> 00:12:45.510
They're the first to know when a
boomer becomes an essential one,

00:12:45.510 --> 00:12:49.780
and no matter what happens, no
matter what method they use,

00:12:49.780 --> 00:12:53.150
they get information and appear at the site.

00:12:53.150 --> 00:12:55.020
I mean that it won't solve any problems,

00:12:55.020 --> 00:12:57.420
no matter how long we wait for
the underground moles.

00:12:57.420 --> 00:13:01.360
I'm thinking of having them search
for the materials for me.

00:13:01.360 --> 00:13:03.660
You mean you'd let the Knight Sabers do it?

00:13:03.660 --> 00:13:06.830
They're an inheritance left by Stingray.

00:13:06.830 --> 00:13:08.460
And I'm going to use them.

00:13:18.410 --> 00:13:18.910
This is good!

00:13:18.910 --> 00:13:19.910
I'm so happy!
This is good!

00:13:19.910 --> 00:13:20.930
I'm so happy!

00:13:22.980 --> 00:13:25.820
Meisio is a very good cook, isn't he?

00:13:25.820 --> 00:13:28.720
Thank you very much, Miss Nene.

00:13:28.720 --> 00:13:30.820
Meisio is happy to hear that from you,

00:13:30.820 --> 00:13:34.550
but if you eat too much, you won't
fit into the hard suit again.

00:13:36.430 --> 00:13:40.830
Nene, how did you get through the
Ministry of Defense fire wall?

00:13:40.830 --> 00:13:42.800
You should have called me Ms. Nene!

00:13:42.800 --> 00:13:45.300
Well, I used a virus that I was raising.

00:13:45.300 --> 00:13:47.800
What?! Is it okay to do things like that?

00:13:47.800 --> 00:13:49.540
Of course not!

00:13:49.540 --> 00:13:52.640
They're probably in bad shape,
trying to recover their system now.

00:13:52.640 --> 00:13:54.510
They might find out you did it, right?

00:13:54.510 --> 00:13:57.050
This girl isn't sloppy like that.

00:13:57.050 --> 00:14:03.520
When I met Nene the first time,
she was sneaking into my system.

00:14:03.520 --> 00:14:05.490
You did some kind of scramble
this time, didn't you?

00:14:05.490 --> 00:14:07.820
No, I didn't.

00:14:07.820 --> 00:14:09.330
Oh, but don't worry.

00:14:09.330 --> 00:14:13.860
They won't suspect the AD Police
of sending stuff like that.

00:14:13.860 --> 00:14:16.870
You must have nerves of steel or something!

00:14:16.870 --> 00:14:19.860
Actually, I just didn't have the time.

00:14:22.040 --> 00:14:23.840
Well, that's...

00:14:25.880 --> 00:14:28.210
Linna, did you have fun at your parents' house?

00:14:28.210 --> 00:14:32.440
Well, yes, but my home is in Tokyo now.

00:14:37.350 --> 00:14:39.960
Hey, Nene, I need your help with
the system downstairs.

00:14:39.960 --> 00:14:41.560
Call me Ms. Nene, okay?!

00:14:41.560 --> 00:14:43.660
I feel strange calling you that.

00:14:43.660 --> 00:14:49.170
It's going to be a trillion years
before you can call me Nene.

00:14:49.170 --> 00:14:52.800
Nene, Nene! Ouch, ouch, ouch!

00:14:52.800 --> 00:14:54.000
About yesterday...

00:14:54.000 --> 00:14:56.010
Thanks.

00:14:56.010 --> 00:14:56.940
What did I just tell you?

00:14:56.940 --> 00:14:58.540
Well, nothing.
What did I just tell you?

00:14:58.540 --> 00:15:00.310
But Nene, it just doesn't feel right.

00:15:00.310 --> 00:15:02.250
Don't give me "it doesn't feel right."

00:15:02.250 --> 00:15:05.770
Nene, that hurts!

00:15:09.290 --> 00:15:11.620
There we go.

00:15:11.620 --> 00:15:14.220
I created this system, but...

00:15:15.760 --> 00:15:18.890
Well, I guess the load might have
become too much for the bus.

00:15:20.400 --> 00:15:23.370
If I put a repeater here at the bridge,

00:15:23.370 --> 00:15:26.500
the response will improve for now.

00:15:26.500 --> 00:15:29.570
Really? Oh, now I see!

00:15:29.570 --> 00:15:34.810
I didn't know what to do when
their circuits got crossed.

00:15:45.620 --> 00:15:48.780
Idiot! You have to do deal with
things like this by yourself!

00:15:50.460 --> 00:15:54.990
I don't have time to waste with a kid like you!

00:16:00.340 --> 00:16:02.200
I wonder if I told you too much?

00:16:03.440 --> 00:16:05.240
Well, thank you, Nene.

00:16:07.810 --> 00:16:08.900
Miss!

00:16:24.260 --> 00:16:25.590
It's too late now.

00:16:26.630 --> 00:16:28.430
Who's that?

00:16:42.510 --> 00:16:44.270
You're Dr. Stingray's...

00:16:47.750 --> 00:16:51.290
I don't know who you're talking
about. You have the wrong person.

00:16:51.290 --> 00:16:53.160
He's my assistant.

00:16:53.160 --> 00:16:56.860
Really? Well, if you say so.

00:16:56.860 --> 00:16:59.300
Anyway, take your time and think about it.

00:16:59.300 --> 00:17:03.230
You're not the type to dirty
yourself with machine oil.

00:17:13.780 --> 00:17:16.210
What the hell are you doing?
Hurry up and come in!

00:17:17.610 --> 00:17:20.320
What did Dr. Mason want?

00:17:20.320 --> 00:17:21.520
Nothing.

00:17:21.520 --> 00:17:23.450
Did you tell him about Sylia?

00:17:32.360 --> 00:17:34.530
Stupid kid!

00:17:34.530 --> 00:17:37.400
I wish he wasn't younger than I am.

00:17:39.370 --> 00:17:41.840
Geez, what am I thinking?!

00:17:43.070 --> 00:17:47.370
What Mason is searching for
underground is the Wiz Lab.

00:17:48.640 --> 00:17:51.280
Papa's lab?! But it was...

00:17:51.280 --> 00:17:53.580
It was buried by the earthquake,

00:17:53.580 --> 00:17:56.950
and it's been missing because of
massive shifts in the Earth's crust.

00:17:56.950 --> 00:17:59.120
He's trying to dig it out? lmpossible!

00:17:59.120 --> 00:18:01.090
I don't know what's there,

00:18:01.090 --> 00:18:05.390
but he's switched over engineers
from the Dragon project

00:18:05.390 --> 00:18:07.730
to the search team for it.

00:18:07.730 --> 00:18:10.330
It can't be! He's looking for that...

00:18:10.330 --> 00:18:12.000
But it was totally...

00:18:12.000 --> 00:18:15.400
That's all I know at this moment. Bye.

00:18:30.250 --> 00:18:31.620
Galatea...

00:18:36.860 --> 00:18:38.550
That's what you wanted me to do, isn't it?

00:18:39.600 --> 00:18:41.130
You're such a good employee.

00:18:41.130 --> 00:18:43.100
It'd be difficult to find another person like you.

00:18:43.100 --> 00:18:46.140
I'm just an investigator.

00:18:46.140 --> 00:18:49.740
I sell my information to the person
willing to pay the highest price.

00:18:49.740 --> 00:18:52.140
It's simply economic logic.

00:18:52.140 --> 00:18:55.010
Your sense of ethics is impeccable.

00:18:55.010 --> 00:18:55.980
Come in!

00:18:58.580 --> 00:19:01.450
Hand a just reward to Mr. Kuzui.

00:19:06.060 --> 00:19:07.860
Cash?

00:19:07.860 --> 00:19:09.690
That's the way I like it.

00:19:26.380 --> 00:19:28.610
Thank you, Mr. Kuzui.

00:19:46.930 --> 00:19:49.160
Sylia's little brother...

00:19:51.130 --> 00:19:54.300
Run search on the family of Sylia Stingray.

00:20:00.880 --> 00:20:01.840
Papa.

00:20:03.250 --> 00:20:04.210
Momma.

00:20:05.750 --> 00:20:06.720
Younger brother.

00:20:12.520 --> 00:20:15.890
Wait a second! When was this picture taken?!

00:20:24.370 --> 00:20:26.700
What is this boy?

00:20:33.080 --> 00:20:36.650
Did you tell Mason about Sylia?

00:20:36.650 --> 00:20:37.610
Shut up!

00:20:38.850 --> 00:20:40.040
Go to bed now.

00:20:56.710 --> 00:20:59.650
Next Episode

00:21:01.820 --> 00:21:04.220
A suspicious town shining in the night.

00:21:04.220 --> 00:21:07.830
It's the place where the one
person who really knows me is.

00:21:07.830 --> 00:21:11.730
Dr. Shang, an old man who calls me "little lady".

00:21:11.730 --> 00:21:13.700
I'm going to search for that disgusting place

00:21:13.700 --> 00:21:16.430
and have it sealed once again.

00:21:16.430 --> 00:21:20.600
Please tell me, Dr. Shang, where that thing is!

00:21:20.600 --> 00:21:22.870
Next Bubblegum Crisis!
